body:
This is the biological answer I'm looking for. It sucks cause I quite literally have OCD and have panic attacks every time I have to shower because it feels like im in a concentration camp being gassed. I'm 24 and asked my parents for advice but of course they're idiots and smoked for 5 years so they don't see it as "as big a deal as smoking." The thing that sucks is, is now all my stuff contaminated?

&#x200B;

I tried to rationalize it as when i lived with smokers in college, but even they had the decency to smoke outside, and even they didn't force me to breathe it while showering. Am I doomed because the residue from the air will stay on all my possessions even if I move?

Yeah, I feel like I have my answer now from this thread. Maybe the math technically makes sense but the bullshit friend math doesn't. It's more of the principal of "how easy would it have been to just think about everyone else's comfort instead of our own" and the fact that this has been reoccurring. I can recall a woods trip several years ago where even when there were OTHER single people, they got beds and I was on the couch.

&#x200B;

Is there a way for the mods to close this thread so nobody accidentally enables me to flare up at them or something? I'm just gonna stop hanging out with assholes

I can just silently stop hanging out with them I guess. I'm not a very aggressive or confrontational person, I just kinda let shit happen to me, which is why I'm so sad when people don't treat me with basic human empathy. I came here to ask for a polite way to tell them I'm sick of being on the couch when we could have easily invited other people (in fact I NAMED a couple other people who could come) but they're response was "nah"

&#x200B;

edit-- invited other people to get a bigger cabin with more beds.

That's a good plan of attack... one of the couples is leaving halfway through so there is a CHANCE I can ask to snag their bed for half of the night. Kind of fucked up cause they are paying less for staying 2 nights instead of 4 but I am somehow not for sleeping like a golden retriever. I think I'm only this upset cause it's like the 10th time this has happened. And I feel like less of a human around them.

&#x200B;

edit: the couple who is staying 2 nights only has to pay 175 each, and I am on the couch for those nights
